HST PDF: the toolbar keeps a clean background with the Windows dark appearance.

With the dark appearance on Windows, the HST PDF toolbar showed stale copies of its controls: a
second outline of the search box with "Se" to its left, the "/ 1" label over that outline, a cut
edge before "Edit in HST Draw", and labels that looked bold (their text painted again over the
old copy). The controls had moved after their first paint, and the pixels they left were never
cleared. The light appearance did not show it.

The viewer is an InterimItemWindow, which is transparent and has no background of its own, so
the area under the toolbar is cleared only when a window below it paints. The viewer now paints
its own background, as the Start Center does, in the workspace colour that showed through before
(on Windows the dialog colour in both appearances, so the light look is unchanged), and repaints
it when the style settings change.

HSTPdfInfo also reports ToolbarLayout, the position, size and preferred size of every visible
toolbar control relative to the toolbar, and ToolbarScreen, the toolbar's screen rectangle. The
runtime checks use them: no control may overlap another or be narrower than it asks to be (cut
off), and the space between controls must be plain background.

